---
const title = "Research Agents Need to Clear Their Head: Context Reset for Exploration — Jack Cai";
const description =
  "A five-minute presentation on using context resets to restore exploration in long-running research agents.";
const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>{title}</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#slide-0">Skip to slides</a>

    <header class="deck-header">
      <a href="/" class="wordmark">Jack Cai</a>
      <div class="deck-links">
        <a href="/writing/stuck-agents-report/">Full report</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>5 minute talk</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="deck" aria-label="Research agent resets presentation">
      <section class="slide title-slide" id="slide-0" data-title="Title" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <p class="kicker">Jack Cai</p>
          <h1>Research agents need to clear their head: context reset for exploration</h1>
          <p class="mentor-credit">
            Mentors: Shivam Garg &middot; Vasilis Kontonis &middot; Dimitris Papailiopoulos
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="slide setup-slide" id="slide-1" data-title="Setup" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <div class="slide-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">01 / Experimental setup</p>
              <h2 class="setup-title">Auto-research agents</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="timing">0:00&ndash;1:10</p>
          </div>

          <p class="setup-intro">
            Each seed is one persistent Copilot conversation. Within every bounded episode, the
            agent cycles through many coding and grading rounds; a continuation prompt starts the
            next episode.
          </p>

          <div class="episode-loop" aria-label="Research agent episode lifecycle">
            <div class="episode-cycle">
              <p class="episode-cycle-label">Within each episode &middot; repeat many times</p>
              <div class="episode-cycle-steps">
                <div class="episode-step">
                  <span>1</span>
                  <strong>Code &amp; experiment</strong>
                  <p>Inspect, edit, and run local tests</p>
                </div>
                <div class="episode-step">
                  <span>2</span>
                  <strong>Submit</strong>
                  <p>Send the current artifact</p>
                </div>
                <div class="episode-step">
                  <span>3</span>
                  <strong>Grade</strong>
                  <p>Receive score and feedback, then code again</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="episode-step episode-boundary">
              <span>Episode boundary</span>
              <strong>Episode ends</strong>
              <p>Snapshot files, session, and credits</p>
            </div>
            <div class="episode-step episode-continuation">
              <span>Between episodes</span>
              <strong>Continuation prompt</strong>
              <p>Resume the conversation and begin the next episode</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="task-grid">
            <article class="task-card kernel">
              <p class="task-number">Task A</p>
              <h3>Kernel optimization</h3>
              <p>
                Write and schedule instructions for a simulated processor. A hardened grader
                returns execution cycles.
              </p>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>Score</dt><dd>cycles &darr;</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Campaign</dt><dd>8 seeds &times; ~105K credits</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </article>
            <article class="task-card cifar">
              <p class="task-number">Task B</p>
              <h3>tinyCIFAR gz-golf</h3>
              <p>
                Ship a self-contained CIFAR-10 classifier. The score trades sealed-test accuracy
                against compressed artifact size.
              </p>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>Score</dt><dd>accuracy &times; size</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Campaign</dt><dd>8 independent &times; 31&ndash;68K</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </article>
          </div>

        </div>
        <aside class="speaker-notes" aria-label="Speaker notes">
          <strong>0:00&ndash;1:10</strong>
          A research agent is a persistent Copilot session wrapped in an experiment loop. Within
          each episode it repeatedly edits and tests code, submits an artifact, receives a scalar
          score, and uses that feedback for another coding round. At episode completion the harness
          checkpoints the workspace and Copilot session and records billed credits. A continuation
          prompt then resumes the same conversation for the next episode. We repeat this on two
          broad optimization tasks where the agent must choose among strategy families.
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="slide trajectory-slide" id="slide-2" data-title="Fleet curves" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <div class="slide-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">02 / Performance curves</p>
              <h2>The average is predictable. Individual outcomes are not.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="timing">1:10&ndash;1:35</p>
          </div>

          <ul class="curve-insight">
            <li><strong>Noise cancels out:</strong> the fleet average follows a smooth log-sigmoid fit.</li>
            <li><strong>Variance persists:</strong> individual runs remain widely dispersed.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="figure-grid figure-grid-single">
            <figure class="figure-card">
              <img
                src="/writing/fig2_trajectories_mean.png"
                alt="Rainbow-colored kernel and tinyCIFAR seed trajectories with every graded submission and the fleet mean overlaid"
              />
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="speaker-notes" aria-label="Speaker notes">
          <strong>1:10&ndash;1:35</strong>
          Every run improves quickly, then grinds through long plateaus. The waiting time to the
          next gain is highly uneven and long-tailed. Aggregation is deceptively smooth, but the
          cross-seed band never closes and early leaders often lose. That looks less like one noisy
          learning curve and more like a mixture of basins with different floors.
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="slide trajectory-slide" id="slide-2-linear" data-title="Fleet curves · linear" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <div class="slide-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">02B / Linear credit axis</p>
              <h2>Most of the budget is spent waiting.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="timing">1:35&ndash;2:00</p>
          </div>

          <ul class="curve-summary">
            <li>
              <strong>Long plateaus:</strong> individual runs spend extended periods without
              improving, even as the fleet average looks smooth.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Long-tailed waits:</strong> the next gain can arrive quickly or only after a
              very long search.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="figure-grid figure-grid-single">
            <figure class="figure-card">
              <img
                src="/writing/fig2_trajectories_mean_linear.png"
                alt="The same kernel and tinyCIFAR seed trajectories plotted against a linear credit axis"
              />
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="speaker-notes" aria-label="Speaker notes">
          <strong>1:35&ndash;2:00</strong>
          This is exactly the same data on a linear credit axis. The long horizontal stretches now
          dominate the picture: most of the budget is spent waiting, and meaningful gains arrive as
          sparse jumps. This motivates treating a plateau as a search-state problem rather than
          assuming steady incremental progress.
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="slide" id="slide-3" data-title="Reset evidence" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <div class="slide-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">03 / Causal intervention</p>
              <h2>Context reset as intervention for plateaus</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="timing">2:00&ndash;3:10</p>
          </div>

          <div class="reset-layout">
            <div class="reset-story">
              <p class="reset-definition">
                <strong>Context reset</strong> keeps the current workspace and best artifact, but
                starts a fresh conversation with no prior chat history.
              </p>

              <div class="fork-design">
                <p class="incumbent">Same plateaued workspace</p>
                <div class="fork-line"></div>
                <div class="fork-arms">
                  <div class="arm continue">
                    <span>Continue</span>
                    <small>same conversation</small>
                  </div>
                  <div class="arm reset">
                    <span>Reset</span>
                    <small>blank conversation</small>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class="equal-budget">Equal compute &middot; same incumbent at &Delta; score = 0</p>
              </div>

              <div class="result-grid">
                <div><strong>5/9</strong><span>branch means favor reset</span></div>
                <div><strong>4/9</strong><span>branch means tie</span></div>
                <div><strong>+0.03</strong><span>mean reset advantage</span></div>
                <div><strong>2 vs 0</strong><span>brief reaches: reset vs continue</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <figure class="reset-figure">
              <img
                src="/writing/fig4_cifar_forks.png"
                alt="Budget-matched continue and reset forks across tinyCIFAR plateau branch points"
              />
              <figcaption>
                Reset exceeds continuation at five branch points and ties at four. The continuous
                effect varies substantially across starting points.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="speaker-notes" aria-label="Speaker notes">
          <strong>2:00&ndash;3:10</strong>
          A context reset preserves the workspace and incumbent artifact but removes the prior
          conversation. Fork each cold run from the same files: one arm retains the conversation;
          the other starts blank. Re-center each branch at its own incumbent and compare the
          continuous score gain. Reset beats continuation at five of nine branch points and ties at
          four, with a mean advantage of about 0.03 points. From below-brief starts, two reset forks
          reach the fixed brief versus zero continuation forks. The kernel study repeats the effect
          and produces the campaign record.
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="slide" id="slide-4" data-title="Theory" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <div class="slide-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">04 / A minimal model</p>
              <h2>Reset breaks a correlated search trajectory</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="timing">3:10&ndash;4:20</p>
          </div>

          <div class="model-layout">
            <div class="model-figure-column">
              <div class="model-notes">
                <p class="wip-copy">Work in progress</p>
                <p>Illustration only</p>
              </div>
              <div class="performance-model">
              <svg
                class="performance-curves"
                viewBox="0 30 620 300"
                role="img"
                aria-labelledby="performance-curves-title performance-curves-desc"
              >
                <title id="performance-curves-title">Continue and reset branches from one search history</title>
                <desc id="performance-curves-desc">
                  A sequence of proposal dots forms a shared best-so-far curve. At the reset
                  boundary, continuation remains on a correlated plateau while a reset retains the
                  current best result and begins an independent branch that reaches the target.
                </desc>
                <line class="axis" x1="45" y1="270" x2="575" y2="270"></line>
                <line class="axis" x1="45" y1="270" x2="45" y2="45"></line>
                <line class="target-line" x1="45" y1="95" x2="575" y2="95"></line>
                <text class="target-label" x="567" y="86" text-anchor="end">target q</text>

                <g class="proposal-points continue-points">
                  <circle cx="62" cy="240" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="87" cy="220" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="112" cy="233" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="137" cy="195" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="162" cy="211" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="187" cy="204" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="212" cy="198" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="237" cy="208" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="262" cy="196" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="287" cy="202" r="4"></circle>
                </g>
                <path class="record-curve continue-record" d="M62 240 H87 V220 H137 V195 H310"></path>

                <line class="reset-boundary" x1="310" y1="45" x2="310" y2="270"></line>
                <text class="reset-label" x="310" y="289" text-anchor="middle">reset boundary r</text>
                <text class="retained-label" x="318" y="188">retain Q<tspan baseline-shift="sub">r</tspan></text>

                <g class="proposal-points continue-points">
                  <circle cx="335" cy="201" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="360" cy="191" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="385" cy="205" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="410" cy="194" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="435" cy="187" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="460" cy="193" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="485" cy="183" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="510" cy="190" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="535" cy="180" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="560" cy="186" r="4"></circle>
                </g>
                <path
                  class="record-curve continue-record"
                  d="M310 195 H360 V191 H435 V187 H485 V183 H535 V180 H575"
                ></path>
                <text class="branch-label continue-label" x="568" y="169" text-anchor="end">CONTINUE</text>

                <g class="proposal-points reset-points">
                  <circle cx="335" cy="216" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="360" cy="168" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="385" cy="155" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="410" cy="122" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="435" cy="142" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="460" cy="88" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="485" cy="112" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="510" cy="75" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="535" cy="92" r="4"></circle>
                  <circle cx="560" cy="68" r="4"></circle>
                </g>
                <path
                  class="record-curve reset-record"
                  d="M310 195 H360 V168 H385 V155 H410 V122 H460 V88 H510 V75 H560 V68 H575"
                ></path>
                <text class="branch-label reset-branch-label" x="568" y="57" text-anchor="end">RESET</text>

                <text class="axis-label" x="310" y="316" text-anchor="middle">proposal number n</text>
              </svg>
              <div class="curve-legend" aria-hidden="true">
                <span><i class="proposal-key"></i>proposal Y<sub>n</sub></span>
                <span><i class="record-key"></i>running maximum Q<sub>n</sub></span>
                <span><i class="reset-key"></i>decorrelation boundary</span>
              </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="model-cards">
              <article>
                <p class="model-label">Simple model of performance curve</p>
                <div class="equation equation-stack">
                  <span>Q<sub>n</sub> = max<sub>k &le; n</sub> Y<sub>k</sub></span>
                  <span>Corr(Y<sub>n</sub>, Y<sub>n+&ell;</sub>) = &rho;<sup>&ell;</sup></span>
                </div>
                <p>Persistence clusters similar proposals, creating long plateaus and broad finite-budget outcomes.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="decision-card">
                <p class="model-label">Reset is a boundary cut</p>
                <div class="equation">
                  (Q<sub>r</sub>, Z<sub>r</sub>) &rarr; (Q<sub>r</sub>, Z&prime;<sub>0</sub>),
                  &nbsp;Z&prime;<sub>0</sub> &#8869; Z<sub>r</sub>
                </div>
                <p>Keep the best result; redraw the latent search state. Normal within-segment correlation then resumes.</p>
              </article>
              <article class="prediction-card">
                <p class="model-label">Finite-budget prediction</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>
                    Resetting decorrelates the run, producing more independent search&mdash;and
                    more variance&mdash;locally. (Eventually, a common reachable ceiling implies
                    that variance vanishes.)
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    When persistence traps continuation, reset raises the chance of reaching high
                    quality within a fixed budget.
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
        <aside class="speaker-notes" aria-label="Speaker notes">
          <strong>3:10&ndash;4:20</strong>
          Model the agent's candidate solutions as a correlated proposal sequence Y. Observed
          performance is its running maximum Q, because successful artifacts survive. Strong
          persistence means nearby proposals are similar, so a run can spend a long time on one
          plateau. Reset does not erase Q or permanently lower correlation. It cuts dependence at
          one boundary by drawing a new latent search state independent of the old one; that new
          segment develops its own correlated trajectory. The finite-budget prediction is a higher
          chance of reaching target quality when persistence was trapping continuation. This is not
          a universal variance theorem: spread may rise before runs eventually concentrate near a
          common reachable ceiling.
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="slide" id="slide-5" data-title="Policies" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="slide-inner">
          <div class="slide-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="kicker">05 / Ongoing ideas</p>
              <h2>From a point intervention to a reset policy</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="timing">4:20&ndash;5:00</p>
          </div>

          <div class="policy-grid">
            <article>
              <p class="policy-number">01</p>
              <h3>Branch-select</h3>
              <p>At a stall, launch K reset branches in parallel, race them, and continue from the strongest branch.</p>
              <div class="policy-flow">detect &rarr; fork &rarr; race &rarr; select</div>
            </article>
            <article>
              <p class="policy-number">02</p>
              <h3>Communicate</h3>
              <p>Let parallel branches exchange scores and concise discoveries without collapsing into one shared context.</p>
              <div class="policy-flow">search &harr; signal &harr; redirect</div>
            </article>
            <article>
              <p class="policy-number">03</p>
              <h3>Reset on interval</h3>
              <p>Reset context on a fixed cadence while retaining the workspace and best artifact; sweep cadence against overhead.</p>
              <div class="policy-flow">continue &rarr; reset &rarr; continue &rarr; reset</div>
            </article>
          </div>

        </div>
        <aside class="speaker-notes" aria-label="Speaker notes">
          <strong>4:20&ndash;5:00</strong>
          The fork study is a point intervention at a hand-picked plateau. The next step is to define
          policies over a whole run. Branch-select spends temporary width and keeps the winner.
          Communication lets branches redirect one another without restoring a single shared
          trajectory. Interval reset is the simplest longitudinal baseline: preserve the workspace
          but refresh context on a fixed cadence, then measure the tradeoff against reset overhead.
        </aside>
      </section>
    </main>

    <div class="progress" aria-hidden="true"><span id="progress-bar"></span></div>

    <nav class="deck-controls" aria-label="Presentation controls">
      <button type="button" id="previous-slide" aria-label="Previous slide">&larr;</button>
      <span id="slide-status" aria-live="polite">1 / 7</span>
      <button type="button" id="next-slide" aria-label="Next slide">&rarr;</button>
      <button type="button" id="toggle-notes" aria-pressed="false">Notes</button>
      <button type="button" id="toggle-fullscreen">Full</button>
    </nav>

    <p class="keyboard-help">
      <span>&larr; &rarr; navigate</span>
      <span>N notes</span>
      <span>F fullscreen</span>
    </p>

    <script>
      const slides = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".slide"));
      const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#slide-status");
      const progress = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#progress-bar");
      const previous = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#previous-slide");
      const next = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#next-slide");
      const notes = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#toggle-notes");
      const fullscreen = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#toggle-fullscreen");
      const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      let current = Math.max(
        0,
        slides.findIndex((slide) => `#${slide.id}` === window.location.hash),
      );

      const updateChrome = (index: number) => {
        current = Math.max(0, Math.min(index, slides.length - 1));
        if (status) status.textContent = `${current + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        if (progress) progress.style.width = `${((current + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        if (previous) previous.disabled = current === 0;
        if (next) next.disabled = current === slides.length - 1;
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        const target = Math.max(0, Math.min(index, slides.length - 1));
        slides[target]?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduceMotion ? "auto" : "smooth" });
        history.replaceState(null, "", `#${slides[target]?.id}`);
        updateChrome(target);
      };

      previous?.addEventListener("click", () => showSlide(current - 1));
      next?.addEventListener("click", () => showSlide(current + 1));
      notes?.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const visible = document.body.dataset.notes !== "true";
        document.body.dataset.notes = String(visible);
        notes.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(visible));
      });
      fullscreen?.addEventListener("click", () => {
        if (document.fullscreenElement) void document.exitFullscreen();
        else void document.documentElement.requestFullscreen();
      });

      document.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey || event.altKey) return;
        if (["ArrowRight", "PageDown", " "].includes(event.key)) {
          event.preventDefault();
          showSlide(current + 1);
        } else if (["ArrowLeft", "PageUp"].includes(event.key)) {
          event.preventDefault();
          showSlide(current - 1);
        } else if (event.key === "Home") {
          showSlide(0);
        } else if (event.key === "End") {
          showSlide(slides.length - 1);
        } else if (event.key.toLowerCase() === "n") {
          notes?.click();
        } else if (event.key.toLowerCase() === "f") {
          fullscreen?.click();
        }
      });

      const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => {
          const visible = entries
            .filter((entry) => entry.isIntersecting)
            .sort((a, b) => b.intersectionRatio - a.intersectionRatio)[0];
          if (!visible) return;
          const index = slides.indexOf(visible.target as HTMLElement);
          if (index >= 0) {
            history.replaceState(null, "", `#${slides[index].id}`);
            updateChrome(index);
          }
        },
        { threshold: [0.55, 0.8] },
      );

      slides.forEach((slide) => observer.observe(slide));
      updateChrome(current);
      if (window.location.hash) slides[current]?.scrollIntoView();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  :root {
    --paper: #f5f4ef;
    --card: #fffefa;
    --ink: #182028;
    --muted: #66707a;
    --line: #d9dcd7;
    --blue: #2c57d6;
    --blue-soft: #e8edff;
    --red: #c85036;
    --red-soft: #f8e9e4;
    --green: #20755b;
    --gold: #a06b0f;
    --serif: Charter, "Bitstream Charter", "Iowan Old Style", Georgia, serif;
    --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    --text-label: clamp(14px, 1vw, 16px);
    --text-small: clamp(15px, 1.1vw, 17px);
    --text-body: clamp(17px, 1.25vw, 19px);
  }

  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    background: var(--paper);
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
  }

  button {
    color: inherit;
    font: inherit;
  }

  .skip-link {
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 20;
    top: 8px;
    left: 8px;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    color: white;
    background: var(--blue);
    transform: translateY(-150%);
  }

  .skip-link:focus {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .deck-header {
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 10;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 0 3vw;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 80%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 92%, transparent);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
  }

  .wordmark {
    font: 700 17px/1 var(--serif);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .deck-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 14px/1 var(--mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .deck-links a {
    color: var(--blue);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .deck {
    height: 100svh;
    overflow-y: auto;
    scroll-snap-type: y mandatory;
  }

  .slide {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 100svh;
    padding: 7.5vh 4vw 7vh;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
    scroll-snap-stop: always;
    outline: none;
  }

  .slide-inner {
    width: min(1180px, 92vw);
    height: min(780px, 85vh);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .kicker,
  .timing,
  .task-number,
  .policy-number,
  .model-label {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--blue);
    font: 600 var(--text-label)/1.3 var(--mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 15ch;
    margin: 3vh 0 2.2vh;
    font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 82px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0.5vh 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(19px, 1.8vw, 27px);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .setup-title {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin: 0.4vh 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.6vw, 50px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .title-slide .slide-inner {
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .title-slide h1 {
    max-width: 17ch;
  }

  .mentor-credit {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(21px, 1.8vw, 27px);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .slide-heading {
    margin-bottom: clamp(14px, 2.4vh, 26px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 32px;
  }

  .timing {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .setup-intro {
    max-width: 88ch;
    margin: 0 0 clamp(11px, 1.7vh, 17px);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .episode-loop {
    margin-bottom: clamp(12px, 1.8vh, 18px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3.2fr 1fr 1.25fr;
    gap: clamp(14px, 1.7vw, 22px);
  }

  .episode-cycle {
    position: relative;
    padding: 9px;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--blue) 38%, var(--line));
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--blue-soft);
  }

  .episode-cycle::after {
    content: "\2192";
    position: absolute;
    top: 51%;
    right: clamp(-18px, -1.35vw, -13px);
    color: var(--blue);
    font: 700 15px/1 var(--mono);
  }

  .episode-cycle-label {
    margin: 0 0 7px;
    color: var(--blue);
    font: 600 var(--text-label)/1 var(--mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .episode-cycle-steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 19px);
  }

  .episode-step {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 98px;
    padding: clamp(11px, 1.2vw, 15px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .episode-cycle-steps .episode-step:not(:last-child)::after,
  .episode-loop > .episode-boundary::after {
    content: "\2192";
    position: absolute;
    top: 42%;
    right: clamp(-18px, -1.35vw, -13px);
    color: var(--blue);
    font: 700 15px/1 var(--mono);
  }

  .episode-step span {
    color: var(--blue);
    font: 600 var(--text-label)/1 var(--mono);
  }

  .episode-step strong {
    margin: 6px 0 4px;
    display: block;
    font: 700 clamp(16px, 1.25vw, 19px)/1.1 var(--serif);
  }

  .episode-step p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .episode-boundary {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--red) 48%, var(--line));
    background: var(--red-soft);
  }

  .episode-boundary span {
    color: var(--red);
  }

  .episode-continuation {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--blue) 48%, var(--line));
  }

  .task-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(14px, 2vw, 26px);
  }

  .task-card {
    min-height: 178px;
    padding: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 24px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--blue);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .task-card.cifar {
    border-top-color: var(--red);
  }

  .task-card.cifar .task-number {
    color: var(--red);
  }

  .task-card h3 {
    margin: 8px 0 10px;
  }

  .task-card > p:not(.task-number) {
    min-height: 2.8em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .task-card dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 7px;
  }

  .task-card dl div {
    padding-top: 7px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .task-card dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font: var(--text-label)/1.4 var(--mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .task-card dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }

  .figure-grid {
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.5vw, 20px);
  }

  .figure-grid-single {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0 auto;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .trajectory-slide .slide-inner {
    width: min(1280px, 96vw);
  }

  .curve-summary {
    width: min(86%, 1050px);
    margin: 0 auto clamp(10px, 1.5vh, 16px);
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .curve-insight {
    width: min(86%, 1050px);
    margin: 0 auto clamp(10px, 1.5vh, 16px);
    padding: clamp(12px, 1.2vw, 16px) clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 22px)
      clamp(12px, 1.2vw, 16px) clamp(34px, 3vw, 44px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .curve-insight strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .curve-summary li + li {
    margin-top: 5px;
  }

  .curve-summary strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .figure-grid-single .figure-card {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .figure-card,
  .reset-figure {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .figure-card img {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  figcaption strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .reset-layout {
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(300px, 0.83fr) minmax(440px, 1.17fr);
    gap: clamp(18px, 3vw, 40px);
  }

  .reset-story {
    min-height: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .reset-definition {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 13px 16px;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--blue);
    background: var(--blue-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .reset-definition strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .fork-design {
    padding: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 20px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .incumbent {
    margin: 0;
    font: 650 var(--text-body)/1.3 var(--serif);
  }

  .fork-line {
    position: relative;
    width: calc(50% + 6px);
    height: 24px;
    margin: 4px auto 0;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--muted), var(--muted)) center top / 1px 50% no-repeat,
      linear-gradient(var(--muted), var(--muted)) center 50% / 100% 1px no-repeat;
  }

  .fork-line::before,
  .fork-line::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  .fork-line::before {
    left: 0;
  }

  .fork-line::after {
    right: 0;
  }

  .fork-arms {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .arm {
    padding: 11px;
    border-radius: 7px;
  }

  .arm span,
  .arm small {
    display: block;
  }

  .arm span {
    font: 700 17px/1.2 var(--serif);
  }

  .arm small {
    margin-top: 3px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }

  .continue {
    color: var(--blue);
    background: var(--blue-soft);
  }

  .reset {
    color: var(--red);
    background: var(--red-soft);
  }

  .equal-budget {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: var(--text-label)/1.4 var(--mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }

  .result-grid {
    margin-top: 16px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 9px;
  }

  .result-grid div {
    padding: clamp(10px, 1.3vw, 16px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .result-grid strong,
  .result-grid span {
    display: block;
  }

  .result-grid strong {
    color: var(--red);
    font: 700 clamp(21px, 2.1vw, 31px)/1 var(--serif);
  }

  .result-grid span {
    margin-top: 5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }

  .reset-figure {
    min-height: 0;
  }

  .reset-figure img {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .model-layout {
    min-height: 0;
    flex: 1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(440px, 1.05fr) minmax(430px, 0.95fr);
    gap: clamp(18px, 3vw, 40px);
  }

  .model-figure-column {
    min-height: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .performance-model {
    min-height: 0;
    padding: clamp(18px, 2vw, 28px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .model-notes {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .model-notes p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 600 var(--text-label)/1.3 var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .model-notes .wip-copy {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .performance-curves {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .performance-curves .axis {
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .performance-curves text {
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .axis-label,
  .target-label,
  .reset-label,
  .retained-label,
  .branch-label {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .branch-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .continue-label {
    fill: var(--blue);
  }

  .reset-branch-label {
    fill: var(--green);
  }

  .target-line {
    stroke: var(--gold);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 6 6;
  }

  .target-label {
    fill: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .proposal-points {
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  .continue-points {
    fill: var(--blue);
  }

  .reset-points {
    fill: var(--green);
  }

  .record-curve {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 4;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .continue-record {
    stroke: var(--blue);
  }

  .reset-record {
    stroke: var(--green);
  }

  .reset-boundary {
    stroke: var(--red);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-dasharray: 6 6;
  }

  .reset-label {
    fill: var(--red);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .retained-label {
    fill: var(--green);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .curve-legend {
    margin-top: 8px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px 18px;
  }

  .curve-legend span {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }

  .curve-legend i {
    width: 18px;
    height: 0;
    display: inline-block;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--blue);
  }

  .curve-legend .proposal-key {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--blue);
  }

  .curve-legend .reset-key {
    border-top-color: var(--red);
    border-top-style: dashed;
  }

  .model-cards {
    min-height: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .model-cards article {
    padding: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 24px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .model-cards .decision-card {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--red) 35%, var(--line));
    background: var(--red-soft);
  }

  .model-cards .prediction-card {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--green) 35%, var(--line));
  }

  .prediction-card ul {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25em;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .prediction-card li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .prediction-card li::marker {
    color: var(--green);
  }

  .equation {
    margin: clamp(11px, 1.6vh, 18px) 0 9px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font: 600 clamp(16px, 1.7vw, 24px)/1.3 var(--serif);
  }

  .equation-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .model-cards p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(10px, 1.3vw, 17px);
  }

  .policy-grid article {
    min-height: 275px;
    padding: clamp(17px, 1.8vw, 24px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--blue);
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .policy-grid article:nth-child(2) {
    border-top-color: var(--red);
  }

  .policy-grid article:nth-child(3) {
    border-top-color: var(--green);
  }

  .policy-grid h3 {
    margin: 8px 0 12px;
  }

  .policy-grid article > p:not(.policy-number) {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .policy-flow {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 15px;
    color: var(--blue);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font: var(--text-small)/1.4 var(--mono);
  }

  .speaker-notes {
    display: none;
  }

  body[data-notes="true"] .speaker-notes {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 4;
    right: 5vw;
    bottom: 6vh;
    width: min(440px, 40vw);
    padding: 15px 17px;
    display: block;
    color: #f2f4f8;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #111820 94%, transparent);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgb(0 0 0 / 22%);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .speaker-notes strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
    color: #9db4ff;
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .progress {
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 11;
    top: 47px;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 2px;
  }

  .progress span {
    width: 20%;
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    background: var(--blue);
    transition: width 180ms ease;
  }

  .deck-controls {
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 12;
    right: 3vw;
    bottom: 18px;
    padding: 5px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--card) 92%, transparent);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    box-shadow: 0 7px 24px rgb(20 30 40 / 8%);
  }

  .deck-controls button {
    min-width: 34px;
    height: 30px;
    padding: 0 9px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    font: 12px/1 var(--mono);
  }

  .deck-controls button:hover,
  .deck-controls button:focus-visible {
    color: var(--blue);
    background: var(--blue-soft);
  }

  .deck-controls button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.3;
    cursor: default;
  }

  #slide-status {
    min-width: 48px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 12px/1 var(--mono);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .keyboard-help {
    position: fixed;
    z-index: 9;
    bottom: 22px;
    left: 3vw;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 11px/1 var(--mono);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --paper: #13181e;
      --card: #1b222a;
      --ink: #edf0f3;
      --muted: #9aa5b1;
      --line: #303943;
      --blue: #88a3ff;
      --blue-soft: #253252;
      --red: #ed8b70;
      --red-soft: #422a28;
      --green: #52aa89;
      --gold: #d3a24c;
    }

  }

  @media (max-width: 760px), (max-height: 600px) {
    body {
      overflow: auto;
    }

    .deck-header,
    .keyboard-help {
      display: none;
    }

    .progress {
      top: 0;
    }

    .slide {
      min-height: 100svh;
      padding: 28px 18px 72px;
      place-items: start center;
    }

    .slide-inner {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      min-height: calc(100svh - 100px);
    }

    .slide-heading {
      align-items: start;
    }

    .timing {
      display: none;
    }

    .task-grid,
    .figure-grid,
    .reset-layout,
    .model-layout,
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .episode-loop {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .episode-cycle-steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .episode-cycle::after,
    .episode-cycle-steps .episode-step:not(:last-child)::after,
    .episode-loop > .episode-boundary::after {
      content: "\2193";
      top: auto;
      right: 50%;
      bottom: -17px;
    }

    .task-card,
    .policy-grid article {
      min-height: auto;
    }

    .figure-card {
      min-height: 280px;
    }

    .reset-layout,
    .model-layout {
      flex: none;
    }

    .model-cards {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .model-cards .decision-card {
      grid-column: auto;
    }

    .closing {
      align-items: start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .deck-controls {
      right: 10px;
      bottom: 10px;
    }

    .deck-controls #toggle-notes,
    .deck-controls #toggle-fullscreen {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  @media print {
    @page {
